; Program 7.28: Rectifier working into a filter capacitor (m-phase, fig. 7.10)
;   Cut-off angle theta from tg(theta) − theta = A = pi r/(m Rн)  (7.5),
;   found by stepping theta with step h, h -> h/3 on overshoot, until h < eps.
;   K = sin(theta) − theta cos(theta),  B = 1/(sqrt2 cos(theta)),
;   F = pi (1 − cos(theta))/K,
;   D = sqrt(pi (theta (1 + cos(2theta)/2) − 3 sin(2theta)/4))/K,
;   C = (1/m + theta/pi)/(2 kпв f Rн)
;   Then U2 = U0 B, Iвm = I0 F/m, Iв = D I0/m, I2 = sqrt2 Iв (by hand).
; Source: Дьяконов, «Справочник по расчётам на микрокалькуляторах», 1985, p.190-191 (book61.pdf pages 191-192)
; Input: r = R1, Rн = R2, m = R3, f = R4, kпв = R5, eps = R6; angles in radians (Р).
; Output: theta = R0, K = Ra, B = Rb, F = Rc, D = Rd, C in X.
; Scratch: R7 = cos(theta), R8 = step h (later 2theta), R9 = A.
;
; Book example: r = 100 Ohm, Rн = 1000 Ohm, m = 2, f = 50 Hz, kпв = 0,1, eps = 10^-4
;   -> C = 7,29187*10^-5 F, theta = 0,7200122, K = 0,11809036, B = 0,94055459,
;   F = 6,6029987, D = 2,2940527
; @angle rad
; @reg R1=100 R2=1000 R3=2 R4=50 R5=0.1 R6=1e-4
; @run
; @expect X=7.29187e-5 tol=1e-10
; @expect R0=0.7200122
; @expect Ra=0.11809036
; @expect Rb=0.94055459
; @expect Rc=6.6029987
; @expect Rd=2.2940527
;
00: ИП1 ИП2 ÷ ИП3 ÷ Fπ × П9 0 П0
10: 1 П8 ИП0 ИП8 + П0 Ftg ИП0 − ИП9
20: − Fx≥0 12 ИП0 ИП8 − П0 ИП8 3 ÷
30: П8 ИП6 − Fx<0 12 ИП0 Fsin ИП0 Fcos П7
40: ИП0 × − Пa 2 F√ ИП7 × F1/x Пb
50: 1 ИП7 − Fπ × ИПa ÷ Пc ИП0 2
60: × П8 Fcos 2 ÷ 1 + ИП0 × 3
70: ИП8 Fsin × 4 ÷ − Fπ × F√ ИПa
80: ÷ Пd ИП3 F1/x ИП0 Fπ ÷ + 2 ÷
90: ИП4 ÷ ИП2 ÷ ИП5 ÷ С/П
